00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:29,333
When people are afraid of you... you can do anything. Remember that.

2
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:52,666
The Krays is a drama, crime, history film directed by Peter Medak.

3
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Twins Ronnie and Reggie Kray are raised in east London, under the
influence of their hateful but doting mother Violet.

4
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
As they grow up, Ronnie's violent nature takes over,
and Reggie follows his brother's lead.

5
00:31:56,666 --> 00:32:02,666
The two become notorious crime lords who rule over the East End club scene.

6
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
But at the height of their power, the brothers veer into different lives, giving the
older crime bosses a chance to reclaim what the Krays took from them.

7
00:44:43,333 --> 00:44:49,333
Ronald Kray, played by Gary Kemp.

8
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Reggie Kray, played by Martin Kemp.

9
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Violet Kray, played by Billie Whitelaw.

10
01:03:53,333 --> 01:03:59,333
Jack 'The Hat' McVitie, played by Tom Bell.

11
01:10:16,666 --> 01:10:22,666
Rose, played by Susan Fleetwood.

12
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
May, played by Charlotte Cornwell.

13
01:23:03,333 --> 01:23:09,333
The Krays is a 1990 British biographical crime
drama film directed by Peter Medak.

14
01:29:26,666 --> 01:29:32,666
The film is based on the lives and crimes of the British gangster twins
Ronald and Reginald Kray, often referred to as The Krays.

15
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
The film stars Billie Whitelaw, Tom Bell, and real-life brothers (although not twins)
Gary and Martin Kemp, both of whom were members of the band Spandau Ballet.

16
01:42:13,333 --> 01:42:19,333
The film explores themes of gangster, based on
true story, twins, 1960s, gay theme.

17
01:48:36,666 --> 01:48:42,666
The tone is dark and emotional.
